In this talk, I will review my recent attempts in expanding the work of Mattia Cafasso and Sofia Tarricone, in their paper: 'The Riemann-Hilbert Approach to the generating function of the higher order Airy Point Process'. The paper demonstrates how, through an appropriately constructed Riemann-Hilbert problem, one is able to prove a Tracy-Widom type formula for the generating function of occupancy numbers of the higher order Airy point processes. This formula can then, itself, be related to a vector-valued Painlevé II hierarchy. It is my goal to be able to replicate this procedure for a new type of point process, one which is related to the 'non-linear Schrödinger equation'; this time relating it to a vector system of Painlevé IV equations.
